          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Layers and Sockets",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "IP on interface",
                    "sub": "ip",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Route",
                    "sub": "gateway",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DNS",
                    "sub": "dig",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Port",
                    "sub": "ss, curl",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Firewall",
                    "sub": "allows it",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Debug ==bottom-up== in that order",
                "Socket = ==IP + port + protocol==",
                "Service ==LISTEN==s; client uses a random ephemeral port",
                "Ephemeral range: `32768-60999`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bind Address",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Bind",
                "Reachable from"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`127.0.0.1`",
                  "local only"
                ],
                [
                  "`0.0.0.0`",
                  "all IPv4 interfaces"
                ],
                [
                  "`::`",
                  "all IPv6 interfaces"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Works locally, fails remotely",
              "text": "Usually a ==loopback bind==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Can't Connect? Check in Order",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "`ip addr`",
                    "note": "have an IP?",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "`ip route`",
                    "note": "default gateway?",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "`ping 8.8.8.8`",
                    "note": "internet by IP?",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "`dig example.com`",
                    "note": "DNS?",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "`curl -v`",
                    "note": "service answers?",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Works on localhost only?** Check the bind address, then the firewall",
                "**Ping IP works, name fails?** The ==DNS== layer",
                "**Listening vs open?** Listening = process bound; open = also reachable through the firewall"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ip and ss: Interfaces, Routes and Listeners",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ip and ss: Interfaces, Routes and Listeners",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Interfaces and routes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Shows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ip -br a`",
                  "one line per interface: address, ==UP/DOWN=="
                ],
                [
                  "`ip link`",
                  "layer 2: state, ==MAC=="
                ],
                [
                  "`ip route`",
                  "the routing table"
                ],
                [
                  "`ip route get 8.8.8.8`",
                  "route and ==source IP== a packet would use"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`default via X dev eth0` = the ==gateway==, used when no other route matches"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sockets with ss",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ss` replaces `netstat`",
                "`-tulpn` = {blue:T}CP, {blue:U}DP, {green:L}istening, {purple:P}rocess, {orange:N}umeric",
                "Without ==sudo==, other users' processes are hidden"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sudo ss -tulpn",
                "ss -tn state established",
                "ss -tn 'sport = :443'"
              ],
              "note": "listeners, live connections, filter by port"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "tcp LISTEN 127.0.0.1:5432 users:((\"postgres\",pid=812))",
                "tcp LISTEN 0.0.0.0:8080 users:((\"node\",pid=2210))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Local Address:Port",
                "Reachable from"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`127.0.0.1:5432`",
                  "{red:local only}"
                ],
                [
                  "`0.0.0.0:5432` or `*:5432`",
                  "{green:public}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Who listens on 8080?** `sudo ss -tulpn | grep :8080`",
                "**Interface and gateway for an IP?** `ip route get IP`",
                "**Why ss over netstat?** It queries the kernel via netlink, faster; netstat is deprecated"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
